WEBVTT

00:00.700 --> 00:03.921
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.021 --> 00:07.289
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.340 --> 00:10.875
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.909 --> 00:13.878
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.913 --> 00:17.382
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.416 --> 00:20.701
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.735 --> 00:22.269
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.303 --> 00:23.604
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.638 --> 00:25.592
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:33.629 --> 00:35.030
Hey, everyone.

00:35.064 --> 00:36.464
You'll never guess
who I ran into

00:36.499 --> 00:37.766
at the market just now.

00:37.800 --> 00:40.268
Your hairdresser who's
almost dead from cancer?

00:40.286 --> 00:41.720
Ross Fishman.

00:41.754 --> 00:43.737
Your old boyfriend?
The one with the penis?

00:43.771 --> 00:45.521
Peter, would you stop
being so jealous?

00:45.556 --> 00:47.173
I dated Ross 20 years ago.

00:47.207 --> 00:48.324
That's right.

00:48.359 --> 00:50.126
And that means he had
you first, Lois.

00:50.160 --> 00:52.495
I'll always be Scottie Pippen
to his Michael Jordan.

00:52.529 --> 00:56.916
Ladies and gentlemen,
Michael Jordan!

00:56.950 --> 00:58.634
(cheering)

00:58.668 --> 01:00.117
And Scottie Pippen.
(scattered clapping)

01:00.135 --> 01:01.302
FAN:
He's also good.

01:01.336 --> 01:02.970
FAN 2:
Why didn't they do Jordan last?

01:03.005 --> 01:03.971
FAN 1:
Alphabetical?

01:04.006 --> 01:05.256
FAN 2:
Oh, right. That's smart.

01:05.290 --> 01:06.507
You're smart.
But still.

01:06.558 --> 01:08.192
Peter, don't be ridiculous.

01:08.226 --> 01:10.327
Ross' wife was with him,
and in fact,

01:10.361 --> 01:12.495
they invited us all over
for dinner tonight.

01:12.530 --> 01:14.297
Oh, come on, Lois.
I hate that guy.

01:14.332 --> 01:16.148
I don't want to have dinner with him.
Hey!

01:16.182 --> 01:17.583
It's cooked food
in another house.

01:17.617 --> 01:19.934
That's exciting for
life-over women like me.

01:19.969 --> 01:21.569
We're going.
All right, fine.

01:21.604 --> 01:23.887
But I'm gonna stare at
his wife's boobs so hard

01:23.922 --> 01:25.789
that when they both go
into the kitchen together,

01:25.823 --> 01:27.807
it will be discussed.

01:30.828 --> 01:34.397
Ah, the cold car ride through
a dark, suburban night.

01:34.431 --> 01:36.398
Look out the window and
think of death, kids.

01:36.432 --> 01:37.799
It's a-comin'.

01:42.071 --> 01:43.505
Wow, Pam.

01:43.539 --> 01:44.973
Everything smells terrific.

01:45.007 --> 01:46.608
Did you make all
of this yourself?

01:46.642 --> 01:48.375
Yeah, I just got home from work,

01:48.410 --> 01:49.626
put down the lawyer's briefcase,

01:49.660 --> 01:50.893
and put on the chef's hat.

01:50.928 --> 01:52.061
You know how it is.

01:52.096 --> 01:53.730
Nah. She don't do nothing.

01:53.764 --> 01:56.599
So, Peter, Lois tells me that
you're working at the brewery.

01:56.634 --> 01:58.034
I think that's great.

01:58.068 --> 01:59.252
A real job.

01:59.286 --> 02:01.503
Trading futures,
that's not real.

02:01.537 --> 02:04.006
But the money is unreal.

02:04.040 --> 02:05.674
Hey. To real jobs.

02:05.708 --> 02:06.891
That's it, Fishman.
Shirts off.

02:06.942 --> 02:08.526
I want to see who's
got bigger pecs.

02:08.560 --> 02:09.810
Peter!

02:09.845 --> 02:11.245
Well, they look better
when they're oiled up.

02:11.279 --> 02:12.479
Pass the salad dressing.

02:12.513 --> 02:14.731
Oh, no, it's an almost-empty
squeeze bottle.

02:14.782 --> 02:16.783
Hang on.

02:20.121 --> 02:21.087
Eh, it's all out.

02:21.122 --> 02:22.222
There's dressing on that salad.

02:22.256 --> 02:24.239
Give me that salad.

02:25.407 --> 02:27.508
Yeah, who's
the better man now, Ross?

02:28.627 --> 02:30.044
Brian, what are you
doing down there?

02:30.079 --> 02:31.295
They didn't set
a place for me.

02:31.330 --> 02:32.380
Not a dog family.

02:32.414 --> 02:34.415
Oh.

02:36.135 --> 02:37.918
G'way.

02:37.952 --> 02:39.969
G'way, you.

02:43.473 --> 02:45.675
So, Ben, do you go
to James Woods High?

02:45.709 --> 02:46.842
(chortling):
No.

02:46.877 --> 02:48.110
I'm a junior
at The Meadows.

02:48.145 --> 02:49.261
It's a private school.

02:49.296 --> 02:51.930
Oh, do they do it so right
at The Meadows.

02:51.964 --> 02:53.682
Class size is so small.

02:53.716 --> 02:55.283
<i>And they really
know your child.</i>

02:55.317 --> 02:56.617
They care.

02:56.651 --> 02:58.152
Mr. Wiggins rested his thing

02:58.186 --> 03:00.587
on Jen Crosby's shoulder
during a test.

03:00.622 --> 03:03.122
Yes, I'm told James Woods High
leads the nation

03:03.157 --> 03:05.358
in teacher-to-student
"thing resting."

03:05.392 --> 03:07.226
Well, it's family
that really matters,

03:07.261 --> 03:09.328
and no family is
closer than ours.

03:09.363 --> 03:11.647
That's why we love
taking trips together.

03:11.682 --> 03:13.648
Here we are in Machu Picchu.

03:13.683 --> 03:15.649
Is that the topless place
in South Attleboro?

03:15.684 --> 03:17.752
I spat on a chick there
at a work retreat.

03:17.786 --> 03:19.086
Peter, just stop talking.

03:19.121 --> 03:21.222
What? We been places.
They ain't so great.

03:21.256 --> 03:24.258
Well, this year is perhaps
our biggest trip ever.

03:24.292 --> 03:26.193
We're climbing
Mount Everest.

03:26.228 --> 03:27.560
Oh, yeah?
Is that right?

03:27.595 --> 03:29.396
Well, so are we!
We are?

03:29.430 --> 03:31.063
Peter, I highly doubt that.

03:31.097 --> 03:33.098
I mean, no offense,
but it doesn't look like

03:33.133 --> 03:35.234
your family would
be up to the task.

03:35.268 --> 03:36.568
I think he's right about that.

03:36.603 --> 03:38.704
After all, we couldn't even
turn a double play.

03:38.738 --> 03:40.605
All right, Griffins, on the
ground, we're going to second.

03:40.639 --> 03:41.706
Let's turn two here.

03:41.740 --> 03:42.974
Ground ball's
a double play ball.

03:43.008 --> 03:44.342
Play's at second.
Let's look sharp.

03:44.376 --> 03:45.676
Tough "D." Tough "D."
Let's flash that leather.

03:45.711 --> 03:46.827
Head in the game.
Play's to second.

03:46.861 --> 03:48.045
This infield is
the Great Wall of China:

03:48.079 --> 03:49.279
nothing's getting past us.

03:49.313 --> 03:50.981
Good "D" behind you, Bri.
Good "D" all around.

03:51.015 --> 03:52.549
(bat cracks against ball)

03:52.583 --> 03:53.783
(in Stewie's voice):
I'm okay, everyone.

03:53.817 --> 03:55.434
Don't worry, I am okay.

03:55.469 --> 03:56.768
My voice sounds weird,

03:56.802 --> 03:59.320
this is weird, I know,
but I feel fine.

04:03.158 --> 04:05.092
Man, what a bunch of jerks.

04:05.126 --> 04:06.759
Yeah, we should call
Ross and tell him,

04:06.794 --> 04:08.828
"This is the hospital,
and your mom's dead."

04:08.862 --> 04:10.663
And then, he'll be like,
"What hospital?"

04:10.697 --> 04:12.765
And we'll be like,
"Saint Up Yours,"

04:12.800 --> 04:14.834
and then... and then
that's, like, two jokes.

04:14.868 --> 04:15.952
Look, I'm sorry, Lois.

04:15.986 --> 04:17.386
I-I know we can't
climb Mount Everest.

04:17.421 --> 04:19.004
I-It's just, that guy
really got to me,

04:19.038 --> 04:20.571
and I wanted to
stick it to him.

04:20.605 --> 04:22.106
Will you call tomorrow
and make some excuse

04:22.140 --> 04:23.124
that doesn't
make me look bad?

04:23.158 --> 04:24.225
Ooh, I know.

04:24.259 --> 04:25.459
Tell him I'm a
pathological liar

04:25.494 --> 04:27.194
and that I've been
under a lot of stress

04:27.229 --> 04:30.064
because of the child
rape charges I'm facing.

04:30.098 --> 04:31.965
I think we should do it.
What?

04:31.999 --> 04:33.366
Lois, you can't be serious.

04:33.400 --> 04:34.634
Oh, I'm dead serious.

04:34.668 --> 04:36.685
You think I liked sitting there
pretending to be polite

04:36.736 --> 04:38.970
to those people while they
talked down to us like that?

04:38.988 --> 04:40.355
Well, I'm sick of it.

04:40.390 --> 04:43.357
I'm sick of this family
always feeling second best.

04:43.408 --> 04:45.810
I want to do something
we can be proud of.

04:45.828 --> 04:47.245
I want Stewie,
Meg, and Chris

04:47.279 --> 04:49.313
to grow up
with some confidence.

04:49.331 --> 04:51.449
Then don't buy our shoes
at the car wash.

04:51.483 --> 04:54.317
But climbing the world's
most dangerous mountain?

04:54.352 --> 04:55.785
Isn't that a little extreme?

04:55.819 --> 04:56.819
Maybe.

04:56.853 --> 04:58.888
But if the Fishmans
can do it, so can we.

04:58.922 --> 05:01.123
Yeah, we're just as good as them
or any other family.

05:01.158 --> 05:02.191
That's right.

05:02.225 --> 05:03.859
You guys, we're
climbing Mount Everest.

05:03.894 --> 05:05.261
Let's do it!

05:05.295 --> 05:07.696
Yay! I drank seven cups
of coffee at the Fishmans'!

05:07.731 --> 05:08.713
(knocking)

05:09.765 --> 05:11.048
Oh, crap. It's Quagmire.

05:11.082 --> 05:12.332
I don't want him
knowing about this.

05:12.367 --> 05:14.184
He's always trying
to horn in on our plans.

05:14.219 --> 05:15.369
QUAGMIRE:
Hey, what's going on?

05:15.403 --> 05:16.537
You guys up to something?

05:16.571 --> 05:17.704
Shh-shh, kids, don't move.

05:17.739 --> 05:18.705
(doorknob rattling)
Hello?

05:18.740 --> 05:20.340
(knocking)

05:31.953 --> 05:33.553
So we're really doing this?

05:33.587 --> 05:35.388
We're actually gonna
climb Mount Everest?

05:35.422 --> 05:36.606
How are you okay with this?

05:36.640 --> 05:37.857
Well, if we make it
to the summit,

05:37.891 --> 05:40.359
I could pee there,
and then it would be mine.

05:40.394 --> 05:42.862
'Cause the rule is,
the highest pee wins.

05:42.896 --> 05:45.130
Okay, gang, once
we arrive in Nepal,

05:45.164 --> 05:47.581
we'll get all the supplies we
need for the trip up Everest.

05:47.616 --> 05:48.916
Okay, but remember, kids,

05:48.950 --> 05:51.335
the people there have
never seen people before.

05:51.369 --> 05:52.803
So when they walk up to you,

05:52.837 --> 05:54.438
quickly stuff a dollar bill
in their mouth.

05:54.472 --> 05:56.240
And then you can pet 'em
as much as you want.

05:56.274 --> 05:57.708
Is that true, Dad?

05:57.742 --> 05:59.642
Nah, truth is, I don't know
nothing about this place.

05:59.677 --> 06:01.276
I don't even know
why it's called Nepal.

06:01.311 --> 06:02.978
The mountains
look like nipples.

06:03.012 --> 06:05.047
Well, you can't just
call a country Nipples.

06:05.081 --> 06:07.015
What about Nepal?

06:07.050 --> 06:08.750
Ooh, I like that.
Ha.

06:08.785 --> 06:10.402
Shocker: God gets it right.

06:16.375 --> 06:18.358
(car horns honking)

06:18.392 --> 06:20.377
(bicycle bells ringing)

06:22.063 --> 06:24.930
Okay, now, we got to make sure
we've got all the provisions

06:24.965 --> 06:26.365
before we head
up to base camp.

06:26.399 --> 06:28.434
'Cause I don't think there's
gonna be a Star Market

06:28.468 --> 06:29.702
halfway up the mountain.

06:29.736 --> 06:31.270
(all laughing)

06:31.304 --> 06:32.338
Oh, Mom.

06:32.372 --> 06:34.071
That's our local
market at home.

06:34.105 --> 06:35.505
Okay, let's split up

06:35.540 --> 06:37.840
and meet in an hour
in front of The Yak Shack.

06:37.874 --> 06:39.942
And my mom is pounding
on the door,

06:39.977 --> 06:41.978
and I'm like,
"Mom, don't come in here.

06:42.012 --> 06:43.279
I'm yakking off."

06:43.313 --> 06:44.747
MAN:
Boo.

06:44.781 --> 06:47.583
So, I've been carrying this
really promiscuous guide around,

06:47.618 --> 06:48.883
and my back starts itching.

06:48.918 --> 06:50.001
I go to the doctor,

06:50.036 --> 06:51.735
turns out I got sherpies.

06:51.770 --> 06:52.786
PETER:
Ha-ha!

06:52.821 --> 06:54.121
Yeah, I'll meet
you guys here.

06:54.139 --> 06:55.306
I'm just gonna be here.

06:57.442 --> 06:59.777
Peter, I don't think we need
a donkey for this climb.

06:59.811 --> 07:01.678
<i>Of course we don't
need a donkey, Lois.</i>

07:01.712 --> 07:02.895
It's a status thing here.

07:02.930 --> 07:04.147
You, leather man.

07:04.181 --> 07:05.498
You sell me donkey.

07:18.894 --> 07:20.494
I don't know what it is,

07:20.529 --> 07:24.297
but you... have got... it.

07:28.918 --> 07:30.869
(all gasp)

07:40.762 --> 07:43.063
Oh, my God.

07:43.097 --> 07:44.498
It's enormous.

07:44.532 --> 07:46.700
Lois, this is probably a
terrible time to remember this,

07:46.734 --> 07:48.969
but I think I might have
left the weed whacker on.

07:49.003 --> 07:51.003
(engine revving)

07:55.392 --> 07:56.959
Well, look who's here.

07:56.994 --> 07:58.827
I didn't believe you'd actually
follow through with this.

07:58.861 --> 08:00.328
Oh, hey, Fishman.

08:00.363 --> 08:02.197
Hey, listen, on
a scale of one to ten,

08:02.231 --> 08:04.231
how bad is the bathroom
situation up here?

08:04.265 --> 08:06.266
Like, ten is a suite
at the Four Seasons,

08:06.301 --> 08:08.268
and one is
a tied-up raincoat sleeve

08:08.303 --> 08:09.637
at a party in your honor.

08:09.671 --> 08:11.071
Yes, we're here, Ross.

08:11.106 --> 08:13.173
When our family says that
we're gonna do something,

08:13.208 --> 08:14.374
we follow through
with it.

08:14.408 --> 08:16.541
Yeah, in fact, not only
are we gonna climb it,

08:16.576 --> 08:18.543
we are gonna beat
you guys to the top.

08:18.578 --> 08:19.544
(chuckles)

08:19.579 --> 08:20.679
I seriously
doubt that.

08:20.713 --> 08:22.581
Oh, yeah?
Well, so do I!

08:22.615 --> 08:24.149
Yeah, so you watch it, Fishman.

08:24.183 --> 08:26.084
We are gonna beat you so bad,

08:26.119 --> 08:28.320
you'll think you gave
Chris Brown an STD.

08:28.354 --> 08:29.353
Is that what happened?

08:29.388 --> 08:31.121
You're not gonna
beat us to the top.

08:31.155 --> 08:33.523
In fact, you probably won't
even climb Everest at all.

08:33.557 --> 08:34.724
You don't have the nerve.

08:34.759 --> 08:35.892
Like hell I don't.

08:35.926 --> 08:37.394
Getting to the top
ahead of you

08:37.428 --> 08:39.679
is gonna be one of the
greatest moments of my life.

08:39.714 --> 08:42.381
It might even beat graduating
from chiropractor school.

08:42.415 --> 08:44.016
Robert Baker.

08:45.752 --> 08:47.735
Brad O'Bannon.

08:48.904 --> 08:50.905
Anyone.

08:56.461 --> 08:58.295
Okay, the Fishmans are
heading up the North Face,

08:58.329 --> 08:59.596
but I've been studying
this map

08:59.630 --> 09:01.531
and I think we've got a better
chance of beating them

09:01.566 --> 09:02.966
if we go
up the South Face.

09:03.000 --> 09:04.400
Oh, we don't need
a map, Brian.

09:04.434 --> 09:06.368
I got us a GPMS machine.

09:06.402 --> 09:07.569
WOMAN (annoyed):
Go up.

09:07.603 --> 09:09.003
What do you think?
Just go up.

09:09.038 --> 09:10.571
Sorry.

09:10.605 --> 09:12.573
Okay, can everyone
just stop freaking out

09:12.607 --> 09:14.341
and just give me,
like, two minutes?

09:14.376 --> 09:16.343
God!

09:16.378 --> 09:18.745
(crying):
Everyone's always yelling at me.

09:18.779 --> 09:20.380
W... All the questions!

09:20.414 --> 09:22.247
All right, well, maybe
we'll turn you on later

09:22.281 --> 09:23.515
and see how you feel.

09:23.549 --> 09:25.767
She was so nice
in the store.

09:25.802 --> 09:28.103
Well, come on, everyone,
let's get started.

09:33.525 --> 09:35.526
(shuddering)

09:36.528 --> 09:38.928
Brian, I'm not sure
I can do this.

09:38.946 --> 09:41.564
It's chillier out here
than Angelina Jolie.

09:41.598 --> 09:42.866
Something like that.

09:42.900 --> 09:44.817
I-I-I don't know,
I-I-I'm so cold.

09:44.868 --> 09:47.286
She took that sad
old lady's husband.

09:47.320 --> 09:49.371
You're just gonna have to
block out the cold, Stewie.

09:49.406 --> 09:51.173
Picture yourself
in a warm place.

09:51.224 --> 09:52.207
(breathes deeply)

09:52.225 --> 09:53.842
Okay, I think I can do that.

09:53.876 --> 09:56.259
♪ Do you remember ♪

09:56.294 --> 09:59.062
♪ The 21st night of September? ♪

09:59.097 --> 10:03.316
♪ Love was changing
the minds of pretenders ♪

10:03.351 --> 10:06.353
♪ While chasing
the clouds away ♪

10:08.556 --> 10:11.189
♪ Our hearts were ringing ♪

10:11.223 --> 10:15.360
♪ In the key that
our souls were singing ♪

10:15.394 --> 10:16.861
♪ As we danced in the night ♪

10:16.896 --> 10:18.863
♪ Remember ♪

10:18.898 --> 10:23.133
♪ How the stars stole
the night away ♪

10:23.168 --> 10:25.119
♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah ♪

10:25.153 --> 10:27.537
♪ Ba de ya ♪

10:27.571 --> 10:29.005
♪ Say, do you remember ♪

10:29.039 --> 10:30.273
♪ Ba de ya ♪

10:30.307 --> 10:33.109
♪ Dancing in September? ♪

10:33.143 --> 10:34.910
♪ Ba de ya ♪

10:34.944 --> 10:39.598
♪ Never was a cloudy day... ♪

10:40.633 --> 10:43.168
♪ ♪

10:44.203 --> 10:46.187
Do you want the
heat on, sir?

10:46.221 --> 10:47.520
Yes, please.

10:47.555 --> 10:50.540
♪ ♪

11:05.404 --> 11:06.771
Oh, my God.

11:06.805 --> 11:08.573
How are we supposed
to get across this?

11:08.607 --> 11:10.374
W-We have to walk
on those ladders?

11:10.409 --> 11:13.109
Guys, be sure to look
down the whole time.

11:13.144 --> 11:16.646
It's really deep
and freaky and disorienting.

11:16.680 --> 11:20.382
(screaming)

11:20.417 --> 11:21.617
(thud)

11:21.651 --> 11:23.519
Peter! Oh, my God!
Dad!

11:23.553 --> 11:26.621
It's okay! There's a huge pile
of dead bodies down here

11:26.655 --> 11:27.989
that cushioned my fall!

11:28.023 --> 11:29.624
Do any of them seem
like they have

11:29.658 --> 11:31.826
any extra tampons
in their backpack?

11:31.861 --> 11:33.595
Uh, no!

11:33.629 --> 11:35.996
"No," like you checked
and there aren't any, "no"?

11:36.030 --> 11:38.464
Or "no," you're
just assuming?

11:38.499 --> 11:40.333
I-I'm embarrassed.

11:45.055 --> 11:46.538
(shuddering)

11:46.556 --> 11:48.590
Peter, you left
the flap open.

11:48.641 --> 11:50.674
It's like a thousand
degrees in here, Lois.

11:50.708 --> 11:52.892
Close the tent now!
It's freezing!

11:52.927 --> 11:55.545
Headline: "Woman Cold."

12:05.104 --> 12:07.855
(all panting)

12:12.227 --> 12:14.077
My God.
I think I see the Fishmans.

12:14.111 --> 12:16.079
They're down on that ridge.
We're ahead of them!

12:16.113 --> 12:17.230
Well, then
let's keep moving.

12:17.248 --> 12:18.582
You guys,
we can do this.

12:18.616 --> 12:21.234
We can beat them!

12:21.252 --> 12:23.503
Hey, you know, I heard, when
you drink at high altitude,

12:23.538 --> 12:24.670
it hits you even faster.

12:25.839 --> 12:27.121
Whoo! Party!

12:27.172 --> 12:28.590
I love you guys!

12:28.624 --> 12:30.792
You don't know
how much you mean to me.

12:30.843 --> 12:32.260
You think you're better than me?

12:32.294 --> 12:34.245
Why can't you hit a curveball?

12:34.263 --> 12:36.264
(sobbing):
I've done nothing with my life!

12:47.524 --> 12:50.009
Hey, cats, is
everybody cool?

12:50.043 --> 12:51.110
Sammy Davis Jr.?

12:51.144 --> 12:52.510
What are you doing up here?

12:52.545 --> 12:54.279
Whatever Frank tells
me to do, man.

12:54.313 --> 12:57.115
Hey, Sam, get back in here
and carry my golf clubs.

12:57.149 --> 12:58.649
Yas, boss!

12:58.683 --> 12:59.683
(laughs)

12:59.718 --> 13:01.919
Ew. Seems kind of racist,
doesn't it?

13:01.953 --> 13:03.571
No, no, 'cause,
'cause Sammy's in on it.

13:03.605 --> 13:05.321
Okay...

13:05.372 --> 13:08.491
But he's still
carrying the clubs.

13:12.446 --> 13:14.297
This is so hard!

13:14.331 --> 13:16.081
I can't do
this, Mom!

13:16.115 --> 13:17.665
Come on!
Keep pushing, kids!

13:17.716 --> 13:19.000
We're almost there!

13:19.051 --> 13:20.951
I'm feeling nauseous.

13:20.969 --> 13:23.254
I think I got altitude sickness.

13:25.340 --> 13:26.790
Hey, Brian, you want
a pukesicle?

13:26.808 --> 13:29.126
I would love a pukesicle.

13:31.728 --> 13:34.313
(gasps) I can see
the top of the mountain!

13:34.347 --> 13:36.348
Let's move it!

13:59.786 --> 14:01.704
We made it!
I don't believe it!

14:01.755 --> 14:03.673
We climbed Mount Everest!

14:03.707 --> 14:06.374
Isn't it amazing, Brian?
You can see for...

14:06.409 --> 14:08.409
Oh, you're doing
your pee thing, right.

14:08.443 --> 14:10.344
I don't really know
what the point is.

14:10.378 --> 14:12.713
I mean, there's no way
other dogs can smell this.

14:12.764 --> 14:13.981
Trust me, Stewie.
They'll know.

14:14.015 --> 14:16.684
They'll know
the world is now mine.

14:16.718 --> 14:19.153
(sniffs)

14:19.187 --> 14:21.220
(bleep) no way.

14:21.271 --> 14:23.170
Oh, my God, you guys.

14:23.188 --> 14:24.838
I'm so proud
of us all!

14:24.856 --> 14:26.190
We made it!

14:26.224 --> 14:28.559
We proved that
we're not second-best!

14:28.610 --> 14:32.562
ROSS: Well, look
who finally got here.

14:32.613 --> 14:34.147
You, you beat us?

14:34.181 --> 14:35.515
Don't feel too bad, gang.

14:35.549 --> 14:38.617
We only beat you by one hour,
12 minutes, and 43 seconds.

14:38.652 --> 14:41.320
And, quite frankly,
we're bored of it up here.

14:41.354 --> 14:44.256
So you guys enjoy it.
We're gonna head back down.

14:45.391 --> 14:46.758
I hate those guys.

14:46.792 --> 14:48.126
Yeah, me, too.

14:48.160 --> 14:49.744
Come on.
Let's head back down.

14:49.795 --> 14:51.713
At least the hard part's over.

14:51.747 --> 14:53.014
I'm not so sure
about that.

14:53.048 --> 14:55.215
You might want to take a
look at those storm clouds.

14:55.249 --> 14:58.234
(thunder rumbles)

15:03.507 --> 15:04.707
Oh, my God.

15:04.741 --> 15:06.559
Yeah, it looks like
it's closing in fast.

15:06.593 --> 15:07.810
We're all gonna die!

15:07.844 --> 15:09.644
All right, everyone get
into a hilarious pose,

15:09.679 --> 15:11.062
so when they dig out
our bodies,

15:11.097 --> 15:12.363
they'll have a good laugh.

15:14.449 --> 15:17.284
Heh. This guy's
pretty funny.

15:27.594 --> 15:29.008
This is terrible!

15:29.009 --> 15:31.160
The storm keeps
getting worse!

15:31.178 --> 15:32.795
Mom, I can't even see!

15:32.829 --> 15:35.547
And the scarf Brian
called "a gay waste"

15:35.598 --> 15:37.882
makes a rather
important appearance.

15:37.934 --> 15:39.768
I'm so hungry.

15:39.802 --> 15:40.969
Me, too.

15:41.003 --> 15:43.104
I don't know
if I can keep going.

15:43.139 --> 15:44.556
Peter, I still
don't understand.

15:44.607 --> 15:47.107
How the hell can we
already be out of food?

15:47.142 --> 15:48.808
Didn't I tell you
to bring trail mix?

15:48.842 --> 15:50.443
Yeah, but by that
I thought you meant

15:50.477 --> 15:54.047
a set list of totally awesome
tunes, which I do have.

15:54.081 --> 15:56.115
♪ I got the power! ♪

15:56.150 --> 15:58.351
And after this, it's
"Everybody Dance Now"

15:58.369 --> 16:00.118
and after that, it's
"Come Baby Come."

16:00.153 --> 16:01.787
<i>That sounds
like Jock Jams.</i>

16:01.820 --> 16:04.822
<i>It is similar
to Jock Jams.</i>

16:04.856 --> 16:06.407
<i>It is Jock Jams.</i>

16:11.496 --> 16:14.164
You guys, look,
there's something up ahead.

16:16.033 --> 16:17.300
I think it's a person.

16:17.335 --> 16:19.501
Oh, my God,
maybe they have food.

16:19.535 --> 16:21.337
Maybe it's a rescue team.

16:32.481 --> 16:34.766
Oh, my God,
it's Ben Fishman.

16:35.817 --> 16:36.817
Is he...?

16:36.851 --> 16:38.267
Yep. He's dead.

16:38.318 --> 16:40.353
Oh, great. Not only are we
caught in this blizzard,

16:40.387 --> 16:42.989
but there's some maniac up here
freezing people to death.

16:43.023 --> 16:44.774
That poor boy.

16:44.825 --> 16:47.693
We should bury him.
It's only right.

16:47.727 --> 16:50.028
Yeah, yeah, we should, Lois.
You're right.

16:50.062 --> 16:52.696
Or we could...

16:52.730 --> 16:53.781
Could what?

16:53.832 --> 16:55.032
Eat him.

16:55.066 --> 16:56.700
(all gasp)
Brian!

16:56.734 --> 16:59.169
Look, if we don't eat something
soon, we're all gonna pass out

16:59.204 --> 17:01.371
from exhaustion and freeze
to death just like him.

17:02.905 --> 17:04.756
Are we really
considering this?

17:04.791 --> 17:06.625
We're talking
about eating a person.

17:06.676 --> 17:08.793
Yeah, I'm not so sure
about this.

17:11.430 --> 17:12.746
Oh, I thought
we decided.

17:12.764 --> 17:13.798
I'm sorry.

17:13.849 --> 17:18.301
Well... I guess
we don't have a choice.

17:22.523 --> 17:25.225
I am oddly prepared for this.

17:27.893 --> 17:29.527
Oh, God, Peter.

17:29.561 --> 17:31.946
I hope Ben would forgive
us for what we did.

17:31.980 --> 17:35.583
Look, we needed to eat,
the same way birds need to fly.

17:35.617 --> 17:37.819
What do you mean, you don't have
our names on there?

17:37.853 --> 17:40.053
My wife and I absolutely have
to be on this flight.

17:40.088 --> 17:41.722
I'm doing the best
I can, sir.

17:41.756 --> 17:43.222
Do you have
your confirmation number?

17:43.256 --> 17:46.325
I think you'll find all the
information you need on here.

17:46.360 --> 17:48.094
Sir, this is just
a piece of paper

17:48.128 --> 17:50.796
with the word "south"
written on it.

17:50.831 --> 17:52.547
Can I speak to your supervisor?

17:52.581 --> 17:55.550
You guys, there's
someone up ahead.

17:57.303 --> 17:58.720
Ben?!

17:58.754 --> 18:00.120
Ben?!

18:00.138 --> 18:02.056
Oh, my God, it's
the Fishmans.

18:02.090 --> 18:03.757
They look terrible.

18:03.791 --> 18:05.725
(wearily):
Have you seen Ben?

18:05.759 --> 18:07.593
We lost him
in the storm.

18:07.627 --> 18:09.479
We're headed back up
to find him.

18:09.513 --> 18:11.797
I just hope he's not trapped
in some crevice somewhere.

18:11.815 --> 18:14.267
Well, my gut tells me
he'll be squeezing himself out

18:14.301 --> 18:15.800
of a crevice very soon.

18:23.575 --> 18:26.777
Oh! We finally made
it below the storm.

18:26.812 --> 18:28.879
Look! I see base camp!

18:28.914 --> 18:34.583
Yay!
We're gonna be okay!

18:34.617 --> 18:36.085
(thunder crashing)

18:37.704 --> 18:41.090
Wait! We have to go back.

18:41.124 --> 18:43.007
What? What are you
talking about?

18:43.041 --> 18:45.176
Kids, your mom is clearly
delirious from the altitude.

18:45.210 --> 18:47.211
I say we leave her
behind and marry

18:47.246 --> 18:49.146
that hot new assistant
from my work.

18:49.180 --> 18:50.881
Look, Ben freezing to
death was one thing.

18:50.915 --> 18:52.916
We had nothing
to do with that.

18:52.950 --> 18:55.684
But we just let Ross and
Pam walk back up there,

18:55.719 --> 18:57.253
probably to
their deaths.

18:57.287 --> 18:59.488
And you know what?
That's not who we are.

18:59.523 --> 19:01.874
We're the Griffins.
And you know how we win?

19:01.908 --> 19:04.727
You know how we keep
from being second-best?

19:04.778 --> 19:05.944
We do the right thing.

19:05.978 --> 19:08.378
We go back up there
and save them.

19:08.413 --> 19:11.482
Tell me again why we ate
a person before we ate the dog.

19:11.516 --> 19:12.966
(sighs) Your mom's right.

19:13.001 --> 19:16.036
Let's head
back up there.

19:16.070 --> 19:17.704
Plus, if we don't rescue
the Fishmans,

19:17.739 --> 19:19.356
their Jewish god is
just gonna sit there

19:19.374 --> 19:20.990
and make us feel guilty.

19:21.024 --> 19:24.292
You do... whatever you want.

19:27.547 --> 19:29.331
(sniffing)

19:29.365 --> 19:31.199
Over here!
I think I smell 'em!

19:35.837 --> 19:39.005
Oh, my God!
Look down there!

19:41.841 --> 19:44.376
We got to get them out!
They'll die down there!

19:44.394 --> 19:46.177
Well, we've got some rope.

19:46.211 --> 19:47.845
(ice cracking)

19:47.879 --> 19:49.313
Quick, Peter!

19:49.348 --> 19:51.715
You're the only one strong
enough to carry two people.

20:03.276 --> 20:04.726
(gasping)

20:11.000 --> 20:12.616
(grunting)

20:16.571 --> 20:18.755
All right, I got 'em!
Pull me up!

20:18.790 --> 20:21.842
(all grunting)

20:21.876 --> 20:23.459
Peter, we can't do it!

20:23.510 --> 20:25.094
You're too heavy!

20:25.128 --> 20:26.712
Keep going!
You're almost there!

20:31.083 --> 20:33.435
I found a rock I like.

20:36.938 --> 20:38.973
Griffins, I don't know
how to thank you.

20:39.024 --> 20:40.875
We never would have made it
without your help.

20:40.909 --> 20:42.776
Oh, you would've done
the same for us.

20:42.811 --> 20:44.645
There are more important things
than a petty rivalry.

20:45.580 --> 20:47.211
We're just happy
that you're okay.

20:47.311 --> 20:49.144
PAM: Well, thank you both.
You saved our lives.

20:50.287 --> 20:52.614
And Peter, I'll never
forget what you did for us.

20:52.615 --> 20:54.299
You're a good man.

20:54.300 --> 20:57.677
All right, you rest up, get better,
we ate your son. Bring it up!

20:57.678 --> 21:58.678
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru